From 9e5c7bbd56452e5b399464b6de835cbcc13d9c31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:58:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: "Rebuild films from interlaced video", on by
 default

videoplayer.hadesfilmfields (Player > Videos > Processing, advanced level), on by default: a DVD
title or an MPEG-2 file that is a film in the fields of interlaced video is played as the film,
each picture put back together and at its own rate (FieldCadence.h). Off: as Kodi plays it, the
same bytes as before.

The label and the help are core strings 41190 and 41191 in en_gb, translated in Estuary as 33190
and 33191 (es_es, es_ar, es_mx), with the settings they name as Kodi shows them in each language
('Adjust display refresh rate', 'Deinterlace method', 'Off').
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po  | 12 ++++++++++++
 .../language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po      | 12 ++++++++++++
 .../language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po      | 12 ++++++++++++
 .../language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po      | 12 ++++++++++++
 .../language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po      | 12 ++++++++++++
 system/settings/settings.xml                         |  5 +++++
 xbmc/settings/Settings.h                             |  2 ++
 xbmc/settings/dialogs/GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp      |  3 +++
 8 files changed, 70 insertions(+)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 05e93f8..1512596 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -27521,6 +27521,18 @@ msgctxt "#41322"
 msgid "12 bits"
 msgstr ""
 
+#. Hades: label of setting "videoplayer.hadesfilmfields"; translated in Estuary (#33190)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41190"
+msgid "Rebuild films from interlaced video"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of setting "videoplayer.hadesfilmfields"; translated in Estuary (#33191)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41191"
+msgid "Many DVDs, and films on television, store a film as interlaced video: each picture of the film is split into its two fields, and on an NTSC disc some fields or frames are repeated to fill 30 frames a second; on a PAL disc the film is often just marked as interlaced. Such video was deinterlaced at 59.94 or 50 Hz, which softens fine detail and makes motion uneven. With this on, before a DVD title or an MPEG-2 file plays, LibreELEC Hades decodes a few seconds of it at its start and at three places further on. Where they all show the same film, the fields of each picture are put back together exactly as they were, the repeated ones are left out, and the film plays at its own rate (23.976, 25 or 29.97 Hz, with 'Adjust display refresh rate'). Video that is really interlaced, a title that mixes film and video, and anything Hades is not sure of play as before, and a frame whose fields do not match (a cut) is deinterlaced on its own. Nothing is rebuilt where 'Deinterlace method' is 'Off' for a video. Applies to the next video. Off: as Kodi plays them."
+msgstr ""
+
